  "narrative": {
    "intro": "West Virginia has received $70.8M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The state recorded 577 awards, with an average award size of $123K. Obligations fell 96.1% year over year. Fiscal-year history shows peak activity earlier in the decade: FY22 obligations were $1.5B, FY23 obligations were $1.8B, FY24 obligations were $2.1B, FY25 obligations were $2B, and FY26 obligations were $1.8B. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buying agency in FY2027 to date, obligating $44.9M. Ambulance Services is the largest industry by obligations in FY2027 to date, receiving $12.7M. Top vendors in FY2027 to date include AAECON GENERAL CONTRACTING LLC at $3.8M, JAN-CARE AMBULANCE OF RALEIGH COUNTY, INC. at $3.8M, and HAMILTON PACIFIC CHAMBERLAIN LLC at $3.8M. All figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial, covering the fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What changed in federal contracting for West Virginia in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 96.1% year over year in FY2027 to date. The state recorded $70.8M in obligations compared with prior fiscal-year levels that ranged from $1.5B to $2.1B. The award count in FY2027 to date is 577 and the average award size is $123K. The shift concentrates obligations in a much smaller current-year total relative to full prior fiscal years."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and industries are driving FY2027 to date obligations in West Virginia?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs leads buying activity with $44.9M in obligations in FY2027 to date. The Department of Justice follows with $12.1M and the Department of the Treasury with $3.7M. Ambulance Services is the top industry with $12.7M, followed by Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $9.7M and Engineering Services at $7.3M. Several vendors, including AAECON GENERAL CONTRACTING LLC and JAN-CARE AMBULANCE OF RALEIGH COUNTY, INC., each account for $3.8M in obligations."
      }
    ]
  },
